    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federation of seven sovereign provinces, formed in the revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> and governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>.</li><li>Its Baltic trade, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> bank made it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>’s leading commercial power in the 17th century.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rembrandt">Rembrandt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-vermeer">Vermeer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baruch-spinoza">Spinoza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-grotius">Grotius</a> worked there; wars and British rivalry wore it down until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> conquered it in 1795.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1628 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-heyn">Piet Heyn</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> captured an entire Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> fleet off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matanzas">Matanzas</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, a haul that paid the company’s shareholders a large dividend.</p></aside>
    </section>

